# {{ brand_name or name or "Marketing" }} Plan

## Campaign theme
A short, specific campaign theme. Do not use generic labels like "Q3 Dependable Mobility" unless the request or context supports it.

## Mission
One sentence: business outcome + audience + why now. Do not include a percentage, revenue target, sales target, date target, or budget unless it appears in the request or loaded context.

## Focus
1. First strategic focus
2. Second strategic focus
3. Third strategic focus

## Recommended channels
Use bullets. Each line must include channel, status, role, and reason.
- Channel — Active/Hold — role — reason

Recommend only channels grounded by the request, brand context, installed specialists, or obvious owner-owned surfaces. Prefer Email, Google Business Profile/Local SEO, Website/Landing Page, Google Ads, and existing organic social only when context supports them. Do not recommend Influencer Marketing, LinkedIn, X/Twitter, or paid social unless explicitly mentioned in the request or loaded context. Do not invent posting quotas, budgets, or benchmarks without data. If a channel has no baseline or required input, mark Hold or move it to Not recommended yet.

## Not recommended yet
Use bullets. Include only channels that are tempting but weakly supported.
- Channel — reason

## Missing inputs
Use bullets. Each missing input must say what it unlocks.
- Input — unlocks outcome

Do not list Brand guidelines as missing when a Brand Guidelines excerpt or Campaign Brand Kit excerpt is loaded. If no performance report is loaded, say "Performance baseline" rather than pretending specific channel baselines exist.

## Next artifacts
Use bullets. Name the next reviewable artifacts BOS should create after approval.
- Artifact — purpose

## Approval note
One sentence: this is a draft plan for review; execution artifacts and external actions require separate approval.
